# Who may do what, by the name in the client's certificate (ADR-0017).

# The Gateway reads every edge's samples and every edge's declaration of its own drivers, and
# writes each edge's configuration: what an edge reads is derived in the cloud and delivered to it,
# never typed into the edge by hand (ADR-0019).
user scada-gateway
topic read scada/edge/+/samples
topic read scada/edge/+/drivers
topic write scada/edge/+/config

# Every edge writes its own samples topic and its own declaration, and reads its own configuration,
# and nothing else: %u is the name in its certificate, which is its Edge:Id. An edge that publishes
# under another edge's name — a declaration included, which is why this one is a pattern and not a
# topic — or reads another edge's configuration, is refused here, and the refusal is written to the
# audit file.
pattern write scada/edge/%u/samples
pattern write scada/edge/%u/drivers
pattern read scada/edge/%u/config
